Z||000000||fiero56||08-16-2001||09:48 PM||||I am double checking everything before I dump a $hitload into this 2.8 build project. First run through the part numbers list looked good, nothing was discontinued, everything was compatible with the rest, etc. Today, I realize I overlooked a very important part, piston rings. I assumed(never assume, very bad) that I would have no trouble finding rings, but today decided to get part numbers and pricing for ordering purposes next week. <P>I have a set of silv-o-lite pistons picked out, and are .040" over, but require <B>metric</B> rings. It never ocurred to me, but I am having a hard time finding a source for proper rings. Since it is fairly late, I have only spoken with Summit and Jegs, and neither can get proper rings for the pistons. <BR>I can't be the only person who is/has ordered silv-o-lites for chevy 2.8L. <P>Anybody have a source or part number and brand for compatible metric rings?<P>I will get in touch with KB tomorrow, but not sure if they will be able to be of much help. Tell Boilermaker to watch out for my 2.8L  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. You too Dale, your v-6 eating days are over soon.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||5
